Subject: [PATCH 35/43] =?UTF-8?q?test(chexc):=20the=20review=20round=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20inferred=20lists=20on=20values,=20semantic=20form,?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20unchecked=20instantiation,=20CanPerform?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

'infer_ref_value_neg.cj' pins the P0 shape at both formation sites (annotated and not);
'infer_ref_value.cj' is the positive half and also pins the reference edge — a function that only
references a thrower infers the requirement. 'covered_entry_demand.cj' asserts Base alone is
reported and Derived nowhere. 'unchecked_instantiated_value.cj' runs the specialized function
through a clause-free value. The four performs tests follow the 'CanPerform<C>' naming.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
